### 🟡 Medium

#### 3. Poor Naming (all 10 tests)

Every test is named `MethodName_Works`. This tells you nothing about the scenario or expected outcome. When a test fails in CI, `UpdatePrice_Works FAILED` gives no clue what broke. The fixes above demonstrate the `Method_Scenario_Expected` convention.

#### 4. Missing Edge-Case / Negative Tests

The production code has important failure paths that are completely untested:

| Untested behavior | Production line | Risk |
|---|---|---|
| `UpdatePrice` on missing SKU | L14 — `throw new KeyNotFoundException` | Exception path never exercised |
| `GetProduct` for non-existent SKU | L11 — returns `null` | Null-return path never verified |
| `ImportFromCsv` with malformed input | L30-34 — `Split`/`decimal.Parse` | `IndexOutOfRangeException` or `FormatException` unguarded |
| `ApplyBulkDiscount` with fraction ≥ 1 | L23-24 | Prices go negative — possible business logic bug |
| `Search` with no matches | L18 | Empty-list return never verified |

